  "//@types/express": "THE CATALOG RANGE, THE ROOT devDependency AND THE `overrides` ENTRY MUST ALL NAME THE SAME RANGE, AND THAT RANGE MUST STAY ON v4. Every workspace asks for `catalog:`, so the catalog is what those packages declare -- but `@types/express-slow-down` and `@types/express-rate-limit` both request `@types/express: \"*\"`, which resolves to `latest` (v5) and lands BESIDE the v4 the runtime actually uses. tsc then sees two express type identities and fails ~200 lines later in `routes/assets.ts`, `routes/email.ts` and `server.ts` -- files nobody touched -- which reads like an application bug and is not one. The `overrides` entry is what holds the whole tree to v4; the catalog naming a DIFFERENT range was two statements of one fact, and the one that loses is silent. The Dockerfile asserts the property this buys (exactly one `@types/express` resolution in the image) so an unpinned image build fails AT the cause rather than in those three files.",
  "overrides": {
    "basic-ftp": "6.2.1",
    "follow-redirects": "1.16.1",
    "browserslist": "4.28.8",
    "ioredis": "5.11.1",
    "send": "0.19.1",
    "proxy-addr": "2.0.8",
    "source-map-js": "1.2.2",
    "react": "catalog:",
    "react-dom": "catalog:",
    "react-native": "catalog:",
    "@types/express": "catalog:",
    "@types/express-serve-static-core": "4.19.9",
    "@radix-ui/react-slot": "1.2.3",
    "@oxy.so/bloom": "catalog:",
    "markdown-it": "12.3.2",
    "linkify-it": "5.0.2",
    "lightningcss": "1.30.1",
    "@expo/cli": "file:./vendor/expo-native/oxy.so-expo-cli-native-58.1.11+oxy.native.1.tgz",
    "@expo/code-signing-certificates": "file:./vendor/expo-native/oxy.so-expo-code-signing-native-0.1.2.tgz"
  },
  "//dependencies": "@oxy.so/core and @oxy.so/services are root workspace links on purpose: bun's isolated install puts @alia.onl/sdk (it ships TypeScript source) in node_modules/.bun, and its imports of @oxy.so/core and @oxy.so/services/ui/client resolve by walking up to the ROOT node_modules, which otherwise holds neither. Without them accounts `tsc` fails inside the SDK's own files.",
  "dependencies": {
    "@expo/metro-runtime": "~58.0.14",
    "@oxy.so/bloom": "catalog:",
    "@oxy.so/core": "workspace:*",
    "@oxy.so/services": "workspace:*",
    "expo-contacts": "~58.0.7",
    "expo-image-picker": "~58.0.10",
    "expo-splash-screen": "~58.0.10",
    "is-arrayish": "^0.3.4",
    "react-native-worklets": "catalog:"
  }
